ject subclass: #FunctionTransform	instanceVariableNames: 'graph pointRotation function '	classVariableNames: ''	poolDictionaries: ''	category: 'Mathematics-Functions'!!FunctionTransform commentStamp: '<historical>' prior: 0!I am a Function Transform.  I am a function wrapper that can be used to do interesting things with functions.The main reason for my creation is to provide a way to rotate a 2d Function about a line,so that a 3d graph is drawn that isn't a "function" and cannot be graphed with a normal functionbecause it's NOT a function (only one 'y' for every 'x').I am too slow to be useful for transforming cartesian to polar.  Graphing time is increased by 10% - 20%.But I am useful for doing things not possible with functions, like spinning while graphing,or rotating a 2d function about an axis so you can complete the sphere or the like.Transforms do slow graphing a bit, but it's "tolerable" until Moore's Law kicks in.If you just want to move the points around, subclass off FunctionTransform and redefine the transform: methodIf you want to draw multiple points for every single point, subclass and redefine the lineFrom:to: method or the transformLineFrom:to: or whatever I finally decide to call it.!FunctionTransform class	instanceVariableNames: ''!FunctionTransform subclass: #FunctionTransformRotate	instanceVariableNames: 'pointRotators '	classVariableNames: ''	poolDictionaries: ''	category: 'Mathematics-Functions'!!FunctionTransformRotate commentStamp: '<historical>' prior: 0!I rotate a 2d function about the x-axis to form a 3d shape.!FunctionTransform subclass: #FunctionTransformTilt	instanceVariableNames: 'lastTime initialTime '	classVariableNames: ''	poolDictionaries: ''	category: 'Mathematics-Functions'!!FunctionTransformTilt commentStamp: '<historical>' prior: 0!Another quickly thrown together Transform!FunctionTransform subclass: #FunctionTransformTurn	instanceVariableNames: 'lastTime initialTime '	classVar